  "report": "# R007 span-forget: COMPLETED\n\nSeeds: 17, 29, 43, 71, 101. Every seed must hold every coverage and falsifier rule.\n\n- seed 17: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 29: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 43: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 71: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 101: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n\n\nLimitations: the mechanism is lineage revocation plus parent-chained chunk keys, not a mid-sequence eviction primitive; the catalog has none; stale reuse is nearly structural to rule out (a chunk key hashes its parent chain): a pass is the expected outcome, and only the negative control (a StaleDonor probe under a suppressed index update) shows the criteria can fail; tiny seeded random model, CPU reference path, one machine profile: nothing about a trained model, a GPU kernel or a non-deterministic reduction order; the probe is the 256-entry next-token logits vector after a 16-byte suffix at one position, plus the KV-state digest of K and V rows for all prompt positions; a trace outside them (timing, memory, uncached activations) is not covered; canary_logit_shift is an integer count of f32 ulps (0 iff the maximum absolute difference is exactly 0); canaries 16 to 31 never appear in the span; model_pin_mismatches and procedure_mismatches are weak metrics (base checkpoint, topology and the canary generator seed are constants; the rest is read from the backend and the requests built); timings come from one shared cloud container; no capacity claim.\n"
